 10:22:16'),('hint-problem-1126-2-mixed-044-item-6','hint-problem-1126-2','WORD','order','순서','먼저 할 일과 나중 할 일을 볼 때 써요.','The order matters a lot to me.','DIRECT_REFRESH_044',6,1,'2026-04-15 10:22:16','2026-04-15 10:22:16'),('hint-problem-1126-2-mixed-044-item-7','hint-problem-1126-2','WORD','wording','표현, 문장 선택','문장이 길거나 애매할 때 유용해요.','The wording was hard to understand.','DIRECT_REFRESH_044',7,1,'2026-04-15 10:22:16','2026-04-15 10:22:16'),('hint-problem-1126-2-mixed-044-item-8','hint-problem-1126-2','WORD','example','예시','설명을 바로 이해하고 싶을 때 좋아요.','An example helps me understand faster.','DIRECT_REFRESH_044',8,1,'2026-04-15 10:22:16','2026-04-15 10:22:16'),('hint-problem-1126-2-mixed-044-item-9','hint-problem-1126-2','WORD','note','메모','작게 적어 두고 다시 볼 때 써요.','I make a note so I do not forget.','DIRECT_REFRESH_044',9,1,'2026-04-15 10:22:16','2026-04-15 10:22:16'),('hint-problem-1126-3-item-1','hint-problem-1126-3','PHRASE','deal with it','그것을 처리하다','Problem Solving 카테고리의 Following Instructions 질문에서 자연스럽게 써 보세요.','I try to deal with it before it grows.','PROBLEM_PHRASE',1,1,'2026-04-15 02:04:06','2026-04-15 02:04:06'),('hint-problem-1126-3-item-2','hint-problem-1126-3','PHRASE','step by step','차근차근','Problem Solving 카테고리의 Following Instructions 질문에서 자연스럽게 써 보세요.','Step by step, it becomes easier to manage.','PROBLEM_PHRASE',2,1,'2026-04-15 02:04:06','2026-04-15 02:04:06'),('hint-problem-1126-3-item-3','hint-problem-1126-3','PHRASE','what helps me most','나에게 가장 도움이 되는 것','Problem Solving 카테고리의 Following Instructions 질문에서 자연스럽게 써 보세요.','What helps me most is breaking it down.','PROBLEM_PHRASE',3,1,'2026-04-15 02:04:06','2026-04-15 02:04:06'),('hint-problem-1126-3-item-4','hint-problem-1126-3','PHRASE','make it manageable','감당 가능한 크기로 만들다','Problem Solving 카테고리의 Following Instructions 질문에서 자연스럽게 써 보세요.','I try to make it manageable first.','PROBLEM_PHRASE',4,1,'2026-04-15 02:04:06','2026-04-15 02:04:06'),('hint-problem-1126-4-item-1','hint-problem-1126-4','FRAME','When this happens, I first ...','이럴 때 저는 먼저 ...','첫 대응을 말하면 답이 구체적이 됩니다.','When this happens, I first slow down and look at the next small step.','PROBLEM_EXTRA',1,1,'2026-04-15 02:04:06','2026-04-15 02:04:06'),('hint-problem-1126-4-item-2','hint-problem-1126-4','FRAME','A strategy that helps me is ...','도움이 되는 방법 하나는 ...','반복해서 쓰는 대처법을 말할 때 좋아요.','A strategy that helps me is breaking the problem into smaller parts.','PROBLEM_EXTRA',2,1,'2026-04-15 02:04:06','2026-04-15 02:04:06'),('hint-problem-1126-4-item-3','hint-problem-1126-4','FRAME','It becomes easier when I ...','저는 ...하면 조금 더 쉬워져요.','개선 조건을 말해 보세요.','It becomes easier when I give myself a clear starting point.','PROBLEM_EXTRA',3,1,'2026-04-15 02:04:06','2026-04-15 02:04:06'),('hint-problem-1126-4-item-4','hint-problem-1126-4','FRAME','I am still learning to ...','저는 아직 ...하는 법을 배우는 중이에요.','완벽하지 않아도 성찰을 보여 줄 수 있어요.','I am still learning to react less quickly.','PROBLEM_EXTRA',4,1,'2026-04-15 02:04:06','2026-04-15 02:04:06'),('hint-problem-1127-1-item-1','hint-problem-1127-1','FRAME','When it is hard to stay patient in long lines, I usually ...','줄이 길 때 참는 것 때문에 겪는 어려움 한 가지는 ...','문제를 먼저 짚고, 다음 문장에서 대처 방법을 붙이면 자연스럽습니다.','When it is hard to stay patient in long lines, I usually slow down and handle one small step first.','STARTER_PROBLEM',1,1,'2026-04-15 02:04:06','2026-04-15 05:13:16'),('hint-problem-1127-2-direct-043-item-1','hint-problem-1127-2','WORD','queue','줄, 대기줄','긴 줄 상황을 바로 떠올리게 하는 단어입니다.','The queue is long, so I try to stay calm.','DIRECT_REFRESH_043',1,0,'2026-04-15 07:22:11','2026-04-15 10:22:16'),('hint-problem-1127-2-direct-043-item-2','hint-problem-1127-2','WORD','delay','지연, 늦어짐','기다림이 길어질 때의 답변에 잘 맞습니다.','A long delay makes it harder to stay patient.','DIRECT_REFRESH_043',2,0,'2026-04-15 07:22:11','2026-04-15 10:22:16'),('hint-problem-1127-2-direct-043-item-3','hint-problem-1127-2','WORD','crowd','사람이 많은 상태, 군중','사람이 많아서 답답한 느낌을 말할 때 좋습니다.','The crowd makes the line feel even longer.','DIRECT_REFRESH_043',3,0,'2026-04-15 07:22:11','2026-04-15 10:22:16'),('hint-problem-1127-2-direct-043-item-4','hint-problem-1127-2','WORD','boredom','지루함','기다리는 동안 느끼는 감정을 말할 때 유용합니다.','Boredom is the hardest part of waiting in line.','DIRECT_REFRESH_043',4,0,'2026-04-15 07:22:11','2026-04-15 10:22:16'),('hint-problem-1127-2-direct-043-item-5','hint-problem-1127-2','WORD','phone','휴대폰','기다리는 동안 시간을 보내는 방법을 말할 때 좋습니다.','I use my phone to pass the time in line.','DIRECT_REFRESH_043',5,0,'2026-04-15 07:22:11','2026-04-15 10:22:16'),('hint-problem-1127-2-direct-043-item-6','hint-problem-1127-2','WORD','music','음악','마음을 가라앉히는 데 도움 되는 요소로 쓰기 좋습니다.','Music helps me relax while I wait.','DIRECT_REFRESH_043',6,0,'2026-04-15 07:22:11','2026-04-15 10:22:16'),('hint-problem-1127-2-item-1','hint-problem-1127-2','WORD','strategy','전략','Problem Solving 카테고리의 Patience in Long Lines 질문에서 자연스럽게 써 보세요.','A simple strategy helps me respond faster.','PROBLEM_BANK',1,0,'2026-04-15 02:04:06','2026-04-15 07:22:11'),('hint-problem-1127-2-item-10','hint-problem-1127-2','WORD','workaround','우회 방법','임시로라도 문제를 푸는 방식을 말할 때 좋아요.','A small workaround helps me move forward.','ACTIVE_VOCAB_038',10,0,'2026-04-15 02:19:50','2026-04-15 07:22:11'),('hint-problem-1127-2-item-11','hint-problem-1127-2','WORD','clarify','분명히 하다','문제를 더 명확히 보는 과정을 말할 때 써 보세요.','I try to clarify the real issue first.','ACTIVE_VOCAB_038',11,0,'2026-04-15 02:19:50','2026-04-15 07:22:11'),('hint-problem-1127-2-item-2','hint-problem-1127-2','WORD','solution','해결책','Problem Solving 카테고리의 Patience in Long Lines 질문에서 자연스럽게 써 보세요.','I am still testing the best solution.','PROBLEM_BANK',2,0,'2026-04-15 02:04:06','2026-04-15 07:22:11'),('hint-problem-1127-2-item-3','hint-problem-1127-2','WORD','adjust','조정하다','Problem Solving 카테고리의 Patience in Long Lines 질문에서 자연스럽게 써 보세요.','I need to adjust my approach each time.','PROBLEM_BANK',3,0,'2026-04-15 02:04:06','2026-04-15 07:22:11'),('hint-problem-1127-2-item-4','hint-problem-1127-2','WORD','recover','회복하